{"name":"Rapture Blue","hex":"#a7d6dd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rapture","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Extreme pleasure, happiness or excitement.","Alternative letter-case form of Rapture."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cause to experience great happiness or excitement.","To experience great happiness or excitement."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rapture"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rapture","blocks":[{"text":"The Rapture is an eschatological (end-times) concept held by some Christians, particularly those of American evangelicalism, consisting of an event when all dead Christian believers will be resurrected and, joined with Christians who are still alive, together will rise \"in the clouds, to meet the Lord in the air.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Teachings_of_Jesus_40_of_40._the_rapture._one_in_the_bed._Jan_Luyken_etching._Bowyer_Bible.gif/330px-Teachings_of_Jesus_40_of_40._the_rapture._one_in_the_bed._Jan_Luyken_etching._Bowyer_Bible.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rapture"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Teachings_of_Jesus_39_of_40._the_rapture._one_at_the_mill._Jan_Luyken_etching._Bowyer_Bible.gif/500px-Teachings_of_Jesus_39_of_40._the_rapture._one_at_the_mill._Jan_Luyken_etching._Bowyer_Bible.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Teachings_of_Jesus_39_of_40._the_rapture._one_at_the_mill._Jan_Luyken_etching._Bowyer_Bible.gif/500px-Teachings_of_Jesus_39_of_40._the_rapture._one_at_the_mill._Jan_Luyken_etching._Bowyer_Bible.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATeachings_of_Jesus_39_of_40._the_rapture._one_at_the_mill._Jan_Luyken_etching._Bowyer_Bible.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Teachings_of_Jesus_38_of_40._the_rapture._one_in_the_field._Jan_Luyken_etching._Bowyer_Bible.gif/500px-Teachings_of_Jesus_38_of_40._the_rapture._one_in_the_field._Jan_Luyken_etching._Bowyer_Bible.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Teachings_of_Jesus_38_of_40._the_rapture._one_in_the_field._Jan_Luyken_etching._Bowyer_Bible.gif/500px-Teachings_of_Jesus_38_of_40._the_rapture._one_in_the_field._Jan_Luyken_etching._Bowyer_Bible.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.